      "spam": false,
      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "@{58c6cbcffd04b1785f747b6c|full_name} For some communities, having a small secondary piece of text that isn't a chatbox is useful - a few plural friends have looked into doing this to show this info, and have found it's not usable as a way to display this info.\n\nThis is updating maybe once per hour or so, but the problem is the promptness of it, it can take a very long time to show up for others.\n\nThis also affects other other things, like online status and status text for example (this one gets refreshed when you open the menu though, but can also be desynced between menu and nameplate)\n\nAnd unlike a chatbox, it's nowhere near as obnoxious.",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    }
